DGR-04: SCOTCH_dgraphRedist() with a user permutation corrupts the graph (in-place unpacking)
=============================================================================================
redistperm.c (public API; reused from the first attempt and re-read): ring of N vertices, each run
done twice, with the identity order inside parts (control) and with the order reversed inside parts
(user permgsttab, ghost part filled with SCOTCH_dgraphHalo as the manual requires, p_l.tex
sec-lib-func-dgraphredist). mode 0: all vertices to the last process; mode 1: packs of 3 to successive
processes (as in test_scotch_dgraph_redist.c); mode 2: all vertices held by process 0 and sent to the
(empty) last process (the review's example). The redistributed graph is checked with
SCOTCH_dgraphCheck() and its adjacency compared with the ring through the vertex labels.
  mpicc <CFLAGS> -DSCOTCH_PTSCOTCH -I$B/include redistperm.c -o redistperm_<build> -L$B/lib -lptscotch -lscotch -lptscotcherr <LDFLAGS>

Pristine 7.0.17 (INFRA/asan, 32-bit ASan):
  mpirun --oversubscribe -np 2 ./redistperm_pristine32 4 0 2     (the review's reversed 4-cycle)
    ERROR: AddressSanitizer: memcpy-param-overlap ... #1 dgraphRedist2 dgraph_redist.c:469 #3 SCOTCH_dgraphRedist
  mpirun --oversubscribe -np 2 ./redistperm_pristine32 8 0 2
    rank 1: rev=1 rc=0 check=1 bad-adjacency=2  (+ "dgraphCheck: arc data do not match")  <- rc=0, silently wrong graph
  -np 3 ./redistperm_pristine32 40 0 0 ; -np 4 ./redistperm_pristine32 41 1 0 : check=1, bad-adjacency 1..3
  -np 3 ./redistperm_pristine32 30 1 1 (packs of 3): passes even reversed: the receiver's own send
  buffer pads the gap between the destination edge area and the receive buffer, which is why the
  existing test did not catch it and why the new test sends everything to one process.

Patched (commit 0001): all 6 (np x mode x N x base) combinations pass on the 32-bit ASan build
(redistperm_build) and on the 64-bit build (redistperm_build64).

Regression test added to src/check/test_scotch_dgraph_redist.c (second case: all vertices to the
last process with a reversed permutation, same executable and data, no Makefile/CMake change):
  test_redist_new32 (test compiled against patched headers) vs pristine INFRA/asan lib, np=3:
    bump.grf, bump_b100000.grf: ERROR: AddressSanitizer: memcpy-param-overlap, rc=1
  test_redist_new_plain vs $WORK/pristinefi/lib (plain build): "dgraphCheck: arc data do not match",
    "main: invalid redistributed graph (2)", rc=1
  vs patched libs ($WORK/build/lib, $WORK/buildfi/lib): rc=0.
  make check_scotch_dgraph_redist passes on 32-bit ASan, 64-bit and SCOTCH_DEBUG_ALL trees.
